<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rabaul</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rabaul is a town on Blanche Bay at the north-eastern tip of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papua-new-guinea">Papua New Guinea</a>. It became the capital of German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> in 1910 and then of the Australian mandated Territory of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a>. The Japanese seized it in January 1942 and made it their main base in the South Pacific, and volcanic eruptions in 1937 and 1994 devastated the town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rabaul.jpg" alt="Rabaul" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stefan Krasowski from New York, NY, USA · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rabaul_from_Vulcanology_Observatory.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
